Execution-plane findings
- `FsiMcpService` currently builds an Akka client and always routes to one fixed actor path:
  `akka.tcp://FsiExecutionSystem@localhost:8081/user/fsiActor`
- `FsiHost` creates a single actor named `fsiActor`
- `FsiActor` creates one `FsiService` at construction time, so actor lifecycle currently equals session lifecycle

Transport findings
- `Messages/McpActorMessages.fs` already isolates transport-safe DTOs
- DTOs currently lack any multi-tenant routing metadata such as `AgentId`, `HostId`, `SessionId`, `HostKind`

Control-plane findings
- `Program.fs` exposes:
  - `/mcp`
  - `fsiAsyncStatus` resource
  - `/fsi/async/{asyncId}`
  - `/healthz`
- There is no host/session registry query surface yet

SA conclusion
- Keep `async-merge` as execution-plane baseline
- Treat backend abstraction + registries + routing as the true next-layer problem

